	// `activate` switches the Agent TLS certificate to the prepared anchor.
	// While `pendingAnchor.unsyncedAgents` is not zero, `activate` fails with
	// `409` and code `agents_not_synced` unless `force` is set; those agents
	// lose their connection. `cancel` drops the prepared anchor.
	// Enrollment strings created before activation contain the old anchor
	// hash and stop working after it.
	//
	// Takes any type of body and a specified content type.
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /settings/tls/agent/anchor (the `ChangeAgentTlsAnchor` operationId).
